-A checked Scalar prefix can use a matching producer's pending core slot.
-If none exists, ordinary gated pre-dispatch remains available on the original
-idle or pending cores, including consumers with cross-type dependencies.
-The ordinary gate still waits for all input dependencies. Only a selected
-gated handoff prepares arguments on AICPU; other gated tasks prepare them on
-the waiting AICore as usual. Ready tasks retain their CPU-prepared arguments.
+A checked Scalar prefix can overlap the tail of the task already running on
+its normally selected pending core. The local task need not be an input
+producer: local pipeline reuse and input readiness are separate conditions.
+For example, an AIV consumer of an AIC result may overlap an unrelated AIV
+task. Its Wait drains the local tail, publishes the local task's real FIN,
+then awaits the consumer's full-fanin doorbell before ACK and computation.
+
+Core selection, early-resolve marks, dispatch queues, and ACK handling are
+unchanged. Predicated, sync-start, MIX, idle, and unmarked entries retain their
+existing fallback. Only a selected gated handoff prepares arguments on AICPU;
+other gated tasks prepare them on the waiting AICore as usual. Ready tasks
+retain their CPU-prepared arguments.
